Unlike the [student importer](/docs/educonnect-tutorial-import-students), the results uploader does
not care what order your columns are in — you tell it, in the wizard. So you can upload the marking
spreadsheet a teacher already keeps, without reshaping it first.

## Steps

The wizard has seven steps and a progress indicator across the top. You can go back at any point.

1. **Pick file** — choose the workbook.
2. **Pick sheet** — if it has several sheets, choose one. Each is listed with its row count, which is
   usually enough to spot the right one.
3. **Header row** — tell it which row holds your column headings. Marking spreadsheets often have a
   title and a blank row above the real header; this is where you account for that.
4. **Columns** — map each column to what it holds: the student identifier, the marks, and anything
   to ignore. Columns you don't map are skipped.
5. **Matching** — the wizard matches each row to a student in the class and shows you the result.
   **This is the step that matters.** Unmatched rows are the ones to look at: usually a stray space,
   a name spelled differently from the enrolment record, or a student in a different class.
6. **Review** — the final list of what will be written. Confirm the count against your sheet.
7. **Upload** — confirm, and it writes.

## If rows won't match

- Match on **Student ID** rather than name wherever the sheet has one; names are the usual culprit.
- A student who has left, or was never enrolled in this class, will never match. Remove the row.
- Fix the spreadsheet and restart the wizard rather than forcing a partial upload — you can always
  fill in a handful of stragglers by hand afterwards with
  [Add Results](/docs/educonnect-tutorial-enter-exam-results).

